x86: select deterministic entropy timing before setup_data seeds the CRNG

Linux consumes SETUP_RNG_SEED before parse_early_param(). Crediting that seed
calls extract_entropy(), which also mixes random_get_entropy(). Waiting for
the harmony_pvclock early_param hook therefore leaks native RDTSC into the
first CRNG key even when all later timing reads use the virtual clock page.

Recognize the token in the already-populated boot_command_line on this early
path. The existing early_param hook still pins the remaining runtime flags.
A non-Harmony boot retains the native entropy path. Same-seed OCI urandom
replay exercises this ordering; supplying a boot seed alone does not pass it.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a diff under the Harmony
repository's designated guest-kernel patch exception.

---
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/harmony_pvclock.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/harmony_pvclock.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/unaligned.h>
 
+#include <asm/cmdline.h>
 #include <asm/harmony_pvclock.h>
 #include <asm/io.h>
 #include <asm/msr.h>
@@ -111,7 +112,13 @@
 
 bool harmony_pvclock_requested(void)
 {
-	return pvclock_requested;
+	/* setup_data RNG credit precedes parse_early_param(). Its first
+	 * extract_entropy() must already avoid native timing. The boot command
+	 * line has been populated before setup_data is parsed.
+	 */
+	return pvclock_requested ||
+		cmdline_find_option_bool(boot_command_line,
+					"harmony_pvclock") > 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(harmony_pvclock_requested);
 
